{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1009320-boston-consilium-the-combat-zone","id":1009320,"title":"Boston Consilium - The Combat zone","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-28T07:26:29-08:00","id":1009320,"title":"Boston Consilium - The Combat zone","content":"So I'm looking to revive my old Boston mage game under 2e. Basically same players...setting but new characters as well as a time line advance. The combat zone never came up much during the original game but I'm looking to make it more of a focus. I've been reviewing the 2e rules on Demense and for the most part no big changes. Has anyone explored this more in your games? come up with interesting idea's as to why the Demesne is &quot;fading&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T07:49:50-08:00","id":1009328,"title":"","content":"The easiest explanation is probably that it's a type of Supernal Verge with a hidden Iris, but that as the area continues to change whatever events or Resonance or whatever aligned to create it are being corrupted or supplanted.<br /> <br /> Or maybe some Mage way back when managed to excise their Oneiros and render it into a &quot;bubble&quot; in the Fallen (A ridiculously epic act of magic I wouldn't bother trying to explain in mechanical terms), but even Indefinite spells run down eventually and this spell's time is running out.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the heart of a Pangean is involved somehow but hasn't been properly cared for and so its potency is gradually declining.<br /> <br /> Anyway, you've got options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T15:00:51-08:00","id":1009498,"title":"","content":"I don't know about the original cause, but my reading was that the Combat Zone was fading due to simple dissonance. It may be a Demesne, but it still has a large number of sleepers in it, and magi using for open magic warfare means they're far more likely to witness magic, I think that's why there are more banishers there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T23:49:54-08:00","id":1009652,"title":"","content":"What I got from the book was that the Demesne's shrinkage and collapse began with the murder of a native by one of the first settlers. He killed the native because they came to warn him against building there, so either the murder or the city's growth could be responsible. If that led to dissonance, upsetting some delicate balance or the change in resonance the book doesn't say but I would go with which ever you can write an interesting story for.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T05:19:51-08:00","id":1009731,"title":"","content":"In my game i mix it up with the Vault III write up from the mysterium book.<br /> <br /> The combat zone is located over the vault and the Demesne is made with the soul stones that reach to encompass it from underground. Thats also the explanation in my game why the mysterium doesnt care about investigating the combat zone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}